The function is already a single comparison, so there is little to gain here. This version adds `FIT_UNLIKELY`-free branchless intent by comparing explicitly against the typed constant. It returns exactly the same 0/1 value as before.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Field::IsValid(void) const
{
    return static_cast<FIT_BOOL>(static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(profileIndex) != static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(FIT_UINT16_INVALID));
}
```